WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.450
He swept floors at JCPenney

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.950
and wore a thrift-store coat.

3
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.350
When he died, he left $8 million

4
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.150
to a library and a hospital.

5
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.950
His name was Ronald Read,

6
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.350
and he ran a gas station for decades.

7
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.150
He drove an old Toyota

8
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.650
and held his coat together

9
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.850
with a safety pin.

10
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.650
Nobody in his town knew

11
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.450
he owned shares in 95 companies.

12
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.950
He never picked winners.

13
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.750
He just bought good companies

14
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.950
and never sold them.

15
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.350
He started buying stocks in the 1950s

16
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.850
with money from his paycheck.

17
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.350
He bought blue-chip names

18
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.150
like P&G and Johnson & Johnson.

19
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.650
He reinvested every dividend,

20
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.750
year after year, for about 60 years.

21
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.550
By 2014, those small buys

22
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.050
had grown into $8 million.

23
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.850
Wealth isn't about earning more.

24
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.350
It's about buying steadily

25
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.550
and not touching it.

26
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.650
Time did the work he couldn't.

27
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.850
I'm Dimples.

28
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.250
I talk about the things we feel

29
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.750
but never say out loud.

30
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:50.950
Follow for more.
